# JSX Visual Response System - Cursor Rules

## Overview ✅ PRODUCTION READY

The JSX Visual Response System enables Juno's AI agent to respond with rich, interactive React components instead of plain text. This solves the critical issue where the agent would type raw SVG/HTML code instead of creating actual visual elements.

## 🎯 Problem Solved

**Before**: Agent typed raw code like `<!DOCTYPE svg><svg><circle cx="50" cy="50" r="40"/></svg>`  
**After**: Agent responds with `<Circle size={100} color="blue" borderColor="black" />`

## Architecture

### Core Files
```
src/components/ui/
├── jsx-renderer.tsx              # Core JSX parsing and rendering engine  
├── jsx-message-renderer.tsx      # Component library and agent integration
└── jsx-utils.ts                  # Utility functions for JSX detection

src/App.tsx                       # Frontend integration and automatic detection
src-tauri/src/agent/prompts/
├── templates.rs                  # Updated system prompts with JSX instructions
```

### Integration Flow
```
Agent Response → JSX Detection → Component Rendering → UI Display
     ↓              ↓               ↓                ↓
Text/JSX → isJsxContent() → JsxMessageRenderer → Visual Components
```

