## Troubleshooting

### Common Issues

#### JSX Not Rendering
- **Check**: Is the content being detected as JSX? Use browser dev tools to inspect
- **Verify**: Component names are correctly capitalized (React convention)
- **Ensure**: All components are available in the registry

#### Component Not Found
- **Add**: Component to `availableComponents` object in jsx-message-renderer.tsx
- **Import**: Required dependencies and icons
- **Type**: Component properly with TypeScript

#### Streaming Issues
- **Incomplete Tags**: JSX Renderer automatically completes partial tags
- **Timing**: Allow time for streaming to complete before checking rendering
- **Events**: Verify agent stream events are being emitted correctly

### Debug Helpers
```typescript
// Check if content is detected as JSX
console.log('Is JSX:', isJsxContent(content));

// Inspect available components
console.log('Available components:', Object.keys(availableComponents));

// Test component registration
console.log('Circle component:', availableComponents.Circle);
```

## Performance Considerations

### Component Loading
- Components are loaded lazily through the registry
- No performance impact on text-only messages
- JSX parsing only occurs when JSX is detected

### Memory Usage
- React JSX Parser is lightweight and efficient
- Component instances are created only when needed
- Proper cleanup of component references

